 {'id':'employment_repeated_reference_pass','task':'UpdateEmployment','observed':['0x13b8632 gets ID array from0xf3e040 and0x13b8650-0x13b8677 resolves each4byte ID through0x85d7c0 and writes object+0x204=0','0x13b8693 calls0x10bd490 on the same r15 item pointer','0x10bd565 obtains array through0xf3e040 using r13(item)+8;0x10bd580-0x10bd5da resolves4byte IDs through0x85d7c0','0x10bd66b obtains array again and0x10bd680-0x10bd6aa resolves IDs through0xc46bc0'], 'interpretation':'Three nearby passes read an ID-list candidate; first two use the same resolver and item-origin. This is a reuse/locality lead, not proven redundant work: intervening callees may mutate state/list or depend on reset order.','runtime_probe':'Attribute samples and cache-miss/latency to0x85d7c0,0xc46bc0 and both passes with caller stacks; confirm list identity and mutation/order constraints before considering reuse or fusion.'},
 {'id':'employment_hybrid_buffer_lifetime','task':'UpdateEmployment','observed':['0x10bd4a8 loads0x220f0 (139504) and0x10bd4b2 subtracts rax from rsp after helper0x42350c0','0x10c15d0,0x10c14a4,0x10c13b4,0x10c12c4 reference validated RTTI CPdxHybridInlineBufferAllocator for SEmployee,SEmployment and pointer variants','initializer fast paths assign capacity0x100 for value buffers and0x400 for pointer buffers','shared allocator allocate candidates0xc2eb30 and0x630380 use slot+0x38 then returned object slot+8','release candidates0xc2eaf0 and0x630340 skip release if pointer==this+8, otherwise slot+0x38 then returned object slot+0x10','0x10c2ba0-0x10c2bce walks0x180byte elements, releases each nested+0x58 array through allocator+0x68 slot+0x10'], 'interpretation':'Large stack/inline storage intentionally avoids some dynamic allocation; actual fallback allocation is indirect and has shared native dispatch. Do not count every allocator reference or release site as heap traffic.','runtime_probe':'Separate stack-page/sample cost, inline hits, overflow bytes and delegated allocate/release identity per task; confirm lifetime correctness before any pool or retained-buffer design.'},
